-- title:
--   Primes under a supersingular point as Γ(ℓ)-translates of the Gauss prime
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $5\le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, subject to the hypothesis `hι` that there exists a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   **The field $K$.** Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with `hK`: $K$ is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79); that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L$-Laurent series generated by the image under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the function field of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ and group $H=\ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times\big)$.
--
--   **The base ring $A$.** Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain which is a henselian local ring, with $L$ as fraction field (via `Algebra A L` and `IsFractionRing A L`) and with algebraically closed residue field, such that $(q:A)\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), i.e. the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}+\cdots$ of the modular invariant, with $j\ne0$ assumed as an instance. Let $\varpi\in A$ be a uniformiser, $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **The chart and the supersingular point.** Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the subalgebra `chartAlg A ↥K {j}` of $K$ attached to the single element $j$, containing the element `jChartFin A ↥K j` given by $j$ itself. Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with $\ker\varphi=y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those elements $j_0$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve $W$ over $\Omega$ with $W.j=j_0$ has no nonzero point $P$ with $q\cdot P=0$.
--
--   **The point $z$ of the integral model.** Let $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of `fFin` and `fInf`, and let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak X$. Let $\varpi_z$ be the element of the stalk of $\mathfrak X$ at $z$ obtained (`hϖz`) as the germ at $z$ of the global section that $\varpi$ determines through the structural morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk (`hz`). Let $y'$ be a point of `XFin A ↥K j` $=\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` carrying $y'$ to $z$ (`hy'`), satisfying the same supersingularity condition for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ (`hss'`), and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$ (`hy'y`).
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart witness.** Let $W_1$ be a discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ be a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), let $f_1,u_1,v_1\in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1-\big(X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1\big)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`, the latter form being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and let $e_1$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk of $\mathfrak X$ at $z$ with respect to its maximal ideal onto
--   $$S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v_1-f_1u_1\big).$$
--   Write $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the homomorphism $C\to$ stalk at $z$ obtained from the global sections of `ιFin` followed by the germ at $z$.
--
--   **The riders `hW₁`.** The hypothesis `hW₁` is a conjunction of seven clauses. (i) *Constants:* for every $a\in A$, $e_1$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of the section determined by $a$ to $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1a))$. (ii) *Stability of the chart:* for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau\in\operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ with `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ` — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ for $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansion series $p_f,p_g$, $p_g$ having nonzero associated series, all $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the ratio of those series, and every $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the product of $\iota$-applied $\tau x$ with the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$ (the $\gamma^{-1}$-conjugated element) equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k$ (the same conjugate) — one has $\tau(C)\subseteq C$. (iii) *Fixing the supersingular point:* for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and $\tau$ as above, every restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ satisfies $\tau(a)-a\in y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ for all $a\in C$. (iv) *Linear part:* for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ as above preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W_1$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W_1)$ such that: $\theta$ intertwines $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ with the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$; $\theta$ fixes every constant $\mathrm{mkS}(C\,w)$, $w\in W_1$; for each $j_0\in\{0,1\}$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}\,X_{j_0})-\mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_i C(M_{i j_0})X_i\big)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0,\mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$; $c^{q+1}-1\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$; $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ mod $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ for all $i,j$; if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ then $c\equiv1$ mod $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$; and if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c-1\notin\mathfrak m_{W_1}$. (v) *Separation of branches:* for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ such that each $P_i$ omits at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0,\mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$, contains $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$, and contains $\mathrm{mkS}(C(a_i)X_0+C(b_i)X_1+h)$ for some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and of $P_2$ along $\mathrm{toC}$ followed by $e_1$ are distinct ideals of the stalk. (vi) *The anchor (Gauss) branch:* for every prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0,\mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$, containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ and containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(1)X_0+C(0)X_1+h)$ for some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and every $a\in C$: the image $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if for every $n\in\mathbb{Z}$ the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ under $A\to L$. (vii) *Position of the cusp parameter:* there exist a proof that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$, a proof that the resulting element lies in $C$, an element $a_0\in A$ with that element minus $a_0$ in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that: for all $a,b\in W_1$ with at least one of $a,b$ outside $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{\,e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W_1$; and $e_1$ carries $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\text{that element}-a_0))$ to $\mathrm{mkS}\,h$.
--
--   **The prime $\mathfrak p$.** Finally let $\mathfrak p\subset C$ be a prime ideal (`h𝔭`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖ𝔭`), with $\mathfrak p\le y$ (`h𝔭y`) and $\mathfrak p\ne y$ (`h𝔭ne`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist $\delta\in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\delta\in\Gamma(\ell)$ and $\delta\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M') δ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (the property recalled in clause (ii) above, for $\gamma=\delta$), such that for every $a\in C$:
--   $$a\in\mathfrak p\iff \text{for every }n\in\mathbb{Z}\text{ there is }m\in\mathfrak m_A\text{ with }\big(\tau(a)\big)_n=\text{image of }m\text{ in }L,$$
--   where $\big(\tau(a)\big)_n$ denotes the $n$-th coefficient of the Laurent series underlying $\tau(a)$. Thus $\tau$ carries $\mathfrak p$ to the prime of $C$ cut out by integrality with all Laurent coefficients in $\mathfrak m_A$.
--
--   This is the step identifying the primes of the finite chart algebra lying strictly below a supersingular maximal ideal $y$ and containing the uniformiser: each of them becomes, after applying the automorphism of $K$ attached to a suitable $\delta\in\Gamma(\ell)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, the prime describing the Igusa (Gauss) component through the cusp at infinity, characterised by all Laurent coefficients lying in $\mathfrak m_A$. It is used in the analysis of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model at supersingular points, in particular by the statements about valuation subrings, Igusa-type components and Ogg profiles that build on this chart witness.
